From f79e263f4e203839970f860946e352cd36cfd96d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:41:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Heal leftover opponent data, fold OU into Format, launcher
 parity

Three changes shipped together as v1.4.3:

SECURITY: a session that died without its room-close cleanup (app killed,
crash) left the opponent's injected team as the port-3 socket save -- the
next SOLO boot played it, and hosting again could have synced it to a new
guest. Cleanup previously ran only at room close or when the NEXT guest
submission arrived. New XDNetplay::HealLeftoverGuestState() finishes the
guest-team lifecycle standalone (the old heal was gated on a .netplayorig
import stash that template-save hosts never have) and also scrubs stray
NetPlayTemp copies on joiner machines. It runs from every safe boundary:
launcher open, team editor open, solo boot, host start, external join, save
import. Boundaries are guarded by a new room-scoped session flag
(BattleCustomizer::IsNetplaySessionActive, set by BeginSession at room open
on both platforms, cleared by EndSession) -- NetPlay::IsNetPlayRunning alone
is game-scoped and cannot see a lobby, which is exactly when live guest
teams are on disk.

The standalone "$XD OU Fixes" cheats toggle is gone on every platform; the
Format dropdown gains an OU entry (Free / OU / Orre Colosseum). The global
cheats flag is now DERIVED state for XD sessions: PrepareForStart reconciles
it to (style/rules block active || Format == OU) in both directions --
including turning a stale toggle-era value off under Free -- remembers the
pre-session value, and EndSession restores it (written to the Base layer
explicitly, so a mid-game room close cannot strand the restore in the
doomed CurrentRun layer). Solo boots no longer claim the netplay lifecycle:
EnsureGbaConfig uses the new ScrubLeftovers() instead of BeginSession, so
the solo cleanup hook actually runs. OU rooms are tagged "[OU] " in the
public lobby, like "[Orre] ".

Launcher parity: Android seeds the bundled VS-mode memory-card GCI into
GC/USA/Card A (from the build-time Sys asset tree, temp+rename write) and
gains the Practice-vs-dummy switch; public-lobby joins on both platforms now
gate on the XD dump and the official BIOS like every other session path;
desktop's join-by-code checks the game list, and the GBA-controls fix button
no longer fires two dialogs.
